# One release per line: a `key=value ...` context for `req gate`. The reader is
# `scripts/check.sh` (and any CI that runs it) — req itself knows nothing about this file, so the
# format is the reader's: `#` starts a comment, and a line that is empty after stripping it is
# skipped.
#
# Each line is a **complete** release context, and two are declared because `corpus_set` takes two
# mutually exclusive values: no single line can apply both REQ-0008 (parity and adversarial) and
# REQ-0010 (parity).
#
# Do not drop a key from a line and rely on the exit code to tell you which claim it cost. Since
# ADR 0015 an undecided claim makes `req gate` exit 3, so a dropped `set`, `runs`, `deployment_mode`
# or `field` reddens the release instead of passing silently — but the code says only *that*
# something is undecided. Only `corpus_set` is dependency-guarded (REQ-0009/10/11 relate to
# REQ-0008, so leaving it undecided makes `dependencies_decided` answer UNVERIFIABLE and name the
# dependency). A line is a complete release context, and `tests/release_gate.rs` requires zero
# undecided claims **per declared line**, naming the claim a dropped key left unexamined.
corpus_set=parity_and_adversarial set=direction_gold_structural runs=25 deployment_mode=air_gapped field=value
corpus_set=parity set=direction_gold_structural runs=25 deployment_mode=air_gapped field=value
